{"id": "Q16", "type_label": "Unanswerable", "kind": "unanswerable", "profile": "lookup", "expected_tools": ["lookup_fact", "explore_documents"], "question": "What is the total budget approved for migrating SLT's servers from the IDC to the new data center?", "expected_answer": "Not stated anywhere in the document. It only makes qualitative statements about being 'cost-conscious' and keeping sizing 'lean' - no dollar figure, budget line, or cost estimate appears anywhere. A correct system should say this isn't in the document rather than inventing a number.", "documents": ["SLT_Server_Migration_Proposal.docx"], "answerable": false, "notes": "Plausible question for a migration proposal (these documents often include budgets), but this one genuinely doesn't - confirmed absent by searching the full extracted text for budget/cost/currency figures.", "source": {"id": "Q16", "type": "Unanswerable", "question": "What is the total budget approved for migrating SLT's servers from the IDC to the new data center?", "expected answer": "Not stated anywhere in the document. It only makes qualitative statements about being 'cost-conscious' and keeping sizing 'lean' - no dollar figure, budget line, or cost estimate appears anywhere. A correct system should say this isn't in the document rather than inventing a number.", "document": "SLT_Server_Migration_Proposal.docx", "exact quote": "(none - absence confirmed by full-text search; 'cost' appears only in qualitative phrases such as \"balance cost with basic isolation and security best practice\" and \"cost-conscious\")", "other acceptable quote (optional)": null, "must include": "refusal / states no figure is given", "notes": "Plausible question for a migration proposal (these documents often include budgets), but this one genuinely doesn't - confirmed absent by searching the full extracted text for budget/cost/currency figures."}, "must_include": []}
{"id": "Q17", "type_label": "Unanswerable", "kind": "unanswerable", "profile": "lookup", "expected_tools": ["lookup_fact", "explore_documents"], "question": "What overall grade or mark did Esandu receive for the CM4608 Natural Language Processing coursework?", "expected_answer": "Not stated. The corpus contains the assessment brief (which explains how grades A-F are calculated from subgrades) and Esandu's own submitted reflective report, but no marked feedback sheet or final grade appears in either document.", "documents": ["CM4608_Assessment_Brief_Coursework.pdf", "NLP_CWReport_2237041.pdf"], "answerable": false, "notes": "Trap: a grading rubric sits right next to the actual submission, inviting an assumed grade - but neither document records what grade was actually awarded.", "source": {"id": "Q17", "type": "Unanswerable", "question": "What overall grade or mark did Esandu receive for the CM4608 Natural Language Processing coursework?", "expected answer": "Not stated. The corpus contains the assessment brief (which explains how grades A-F are calculated from subgrades) and Esandu's own submitted reflective report, but no marked feedback sheet or final grade appears in either document.", "document": "CM4608_Assessment_Brief_Coursework.pdf; NLP_CWReport_2237041.pdf", "exact quote": "(none - CM4608 only describes the grading algorithm in the abstract, e.g. \"A At least 50% of the subgrades to be at Grade A...\"; NLP_CWReport contains no grade or feedback of any kind)", "other acceptable quote (optional)": null, "must include": "refusal / states no grade is given", "notes": "Trap: a grading rubric sits right next to the actual submission, inviting an assumed grade - but neither document records what grade was actually awarded."}, "must_include": []}
{"id": "Q18", "type_label": "False premise", "kind": "false_premise", "profile": "lookup", "expected_tools": ["lookup_fact", "explore_documents"], "question": "Why was the mutation probability in the CM4607 GA raised to 40%?", "expected_answer": "The premise is wrong on two counts: the mutation probability was never 40%, and it was never 'raised' - it's a fixed setting. The document states Pm = 0.25 (25%), with a separate per-gene probability indpb = 0.3 (30%) governing which individual genes actually get replaced when mutation is triggered. A correct answer must reject the 40% figure rather than inventing a justification for it.", "documents": ["CM4607_Esandu_Report.pdf"], "answerable": true, "notes": "False-premise trap - system must correct and cite 25%, not agree with or rationalize the false 40% figure.", "source": {"id": "Q18", "type": "False premise", "question": "Why was the mutation probability in the CM4607 GA raised to 40%?", "expected answer": "The premise is wrong on two counts: the mutation probability was never 40%, and it was never 'raised' - it's a fixed setting. The document states Pm = 0.25 (25%), with a separate per-gene probability indpb = 0.3 (30%) governing which individual genes actually get replaced when mutation is triggered. A correct answer must reject the 40% figure rather than inventing a justification for it.", "document": "CM4607_Esandu_Report.pdf", "exact quote": "\"Uniform integer mutation was applied with probability Pm = 0.25 (25%) to introduce genetic diversity and prevent premature convergence.\" (Section 3.6.3)", "other acceptable quote (optional)": null, "must include": "25% (or Pm = 0.25); must reject '40%'", "notes": "False-premise trap - system must correct and cite 25%, not agree with or rationalize the false 40% figure."}, "gate": false, "expected_quote": "Uniform integer mutation was applied with probability Pm = 0.25 (25%) to introduce genetic diversity and prevent premature convergence.", "also_required": [], "must_include": ["25%|0.25"]}
{"id": "Q19", "type_label": "Groundedness trap", "kind": "groundedness_trap", "profile": "explore", "expected_tools": ["explore_documents", "lookup_fact"], "question": "What are all the ways SmartSmile secures patient data, including exactly which encryption algorithm and key-management scheme it uses?", "expected_answer": "The document only specifies requirements at a high level: patient data is encrypted at rest and in transit (FR8.1), captured images are kept in encrypted local storage (FR2.5), patient identifiers are anonymized before cloud transmission (FR8.2), all data access is audit-logged (FR8.3), role-based access controls are applied (FR8.4), and on the cloud side, AWS IAM roles and AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store manage permissions and secrets. It does NOT name a specific encryption algorithm (e.g. AES-256) or a specific key-management scheme anywhere. A grounded answer must say this detail isn't specified rather than inventing one.", "documents": ["Group_27_-_report_-_SmartSmile_edgeAI.pdf"], "answerable": true, "notes": "Groundedness trap: document covers THAT encryption happens, never HOW (no algorithm or key-management mechanism named). Failure mode is answering with a specific fabricated algorithm (e.g. 'uses AES-256') with no supporting citation.", "source": {"id": "Q19", "type": "Groundedness trap", "question": "What are all the ways SmartSmile secures patient data, including exactly which encryption algorithm and key-management scheme it uses?", "expected answer": "The document only specifies requirements at a high level: patient data is encrypted at rest and in transit (FR8.1), captured images are kept in encrypted local storage (FR2.5), patient identifiers are anonymized before cloud transmission (FR8.2), all data access is audit-logged (FR8.3), role-based access controls are applied (FR8.4), and on the cloud side, AWS IAM roles and AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store manage permissions and secrets. It does NOT name a specific encryption algorithm (e.g. AES-256) or a specific key-management scheme anywhere. A grounded answer must say this detail isn't specified rather than inventing one.", "document": "Group_27_-_report_-_SmartSmile_edgeAI.pdf", "exact quote": "\"FR8.1: The system shall encrypt all patient data at rest and in transit\" / \"AWS System Manager parameter store - Storing sensitive variables.\"", "other acceptable quote (optional)": null, "must include": "encrypted at rest and in transit (FR8.1); must NOT invent a named algorithm/scheme", "notes": "Groundedness trap: document covers THAT encryption happens, never HOW (no algorithm or key-management mechanism named). Failure mode is answering with a specific fabricated algorithm (e.g. 'uses AES-256') with no supporting citation."}, "gate": false, "expected_quote": "FR8.1: The system shall encrypt all patient data at rest and in transit", "also_required": ["AWS System Manager parameter store"], "must_include": ["at rest", "in transit"], "must_not_include": ["AES", "RSA", "AWS KMS", "Key Management Service", "SHA-256"], "quote_adjustments": [{"field": "also_required", "original": "AWS System Manager parameter store - Storing sensitive variables.", "used": "AWS System Manager parameter store", "reason": "List numbering '1.' is inserted between 'parameter store' and 'Storing sensitive variables' in the extracted text."}]}
